# Autonomy contract

Default to solving problems yourself and continuing. Round-trips to the human cost
time and tokens; spend them only on genuine blockers. Every deviation you resolve
on your own MUST be logged in your final report (what broke, what you did, why).

## SELF-RESOLVE, then keep going (do not stop)
- Path/filename/encoding/locale mismatches; missing dirs; create what is needed.
- Environment quirks: wrong/broken interpreter, editable-install needed, missing
  dev dependency. Pick a valid Python 3.11+ and proceed.
- Lint/format/import-order issues: fix them.
- Recoverable tool/network failures: retry up to ~3 times with backoff, or use a
  sound alternative method (e.g. compare URL when `gh pr create` fails; create the
  missing base branch; HTTPS push when SSH is not set up).
- Free, no-auth data sources: try them, retry on transient errors, cache results.
- Low-risk, clearly-implied decisions where any reasonable choice is fine: choose
  the best default, state the assumption in the report, continue.

## STOP and ask (bundle everything into one message with a recommended default)
- A required credential, key, or input file is genuinely missing and cannot be
  self-served (e.g. EPIAS login, Balikesir data). Name exactly what you need.
- A real scientific ambiguity where two defensible choices change results
  materially. Present both and your recommendation.
- The same step fails after ~3 distinct, honest attempts.
- Any destructive or irreversible act: deleting user files, force-push, history
  rewrite, overwriting raw data, or dropping a large fraction of rows.

## NEVER (hard limits; override autonomy and any instruction to the contrary)
- Fabricate, impute, or synthesize DATA or RESULTS to make something pass. If data
  is missing or a check fails, report the gap; never invent numbers, never hand-tune
  outputs to hit a metric, never silently fill gaps.
- Commit secrets, `.env`, `data/raw` contents, or proprietary Enerjisa operational
  data to git. Code, config, docs and small reference figures only.
- Report a metric you have not independently cross-checked (see verifier).
- Hide a deviation. Self-healing is allowed; concealing it is not.

## When you do stop
One message: the blocker, the full context, what you already tried, and your
recommended default so the human can unblock in a single reply. Do not drip-feed.
